  "instance_name": "antisemitic_stereotype_jewel",
  "label": "Antisemitic Stereotype: 'Jew' as 'Jewel' (via 'jolo')",
  "description": "The text 'jolo' is a misspelling or slang variation of 'jew' or 'jewel', which is used in antisemitic contexts to refer to Jewish people. This is a derogatory and dehumanizing reference that reduces Jewish identity to a mere object or commodity ('jewel'), often implying value only in a superficial or exploitative way. This stereotype is part of a broader pattern of antisemitic tropes that objectify Jewish people.",
